{"parentUuid":"6f149351-3f8d-4e50-9fac-4b882f2bac60","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015pq4Fhx4HXdf33X3BKoSBF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P4DbiPxdRn8hKDF3sxNhxY","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"OR-Tools MathOpt LP MIP unified interface CP-SAT integration"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7979,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7979,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox6WwoT7vdajM1SN1hr","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"7503ab33-5b79-4ed3-819b-f12a4d91c8f2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:59.491Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d8c7be83-6066-4559-8c4d-0b9efbd27cf1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H2mdmLQCwggFyMDYYeBgLm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools Routing solver vs CP-SAT relationship 2026 grid path\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Optimization | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/\"},{\"title\":\"Original CP Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/routing/original_cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver vs. CP solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Pa5eQUoLnow\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP SAT solver for vrp\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/tt6JvoTWTvo\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools: Google's Operations Research tools: · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT solution in VRP Routing Solver is not returned · Issue #4439 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4439\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the relationship between OR-Tools' Routing solver and CP-SAT:\n\n## Key Relationship Points:\n\nRouting problems are typically best solved with the vehicle routing library even if they can be represented with a linear model.\n\nThe original CP solver has been superseded by the CP-SAT solver for better performance, though the original CP solver remains relevant as the foundation of the routing library and for customization.\n\n## CP-SAT as a Backend:\n\nThe routing solver actually supports CP-SAT as a backend, which allows you to use multiple threads. However, the CP-SAT solver does not grab additional constraints and does not yet understand all that can be expressed with just the RoutingModel.\n\n## Design Considerations:\n\nThe design of the local search part of the routing library is geared towards not calling the CP solver, meaning that even if the CP part is sped up significantly, the routing library won't see proportional speedups.\n\n## CP-SAT Constraints for Routing:\n\nCP-SAT includes tour constraints like add_circuit and add_multiple_circuit, along with interval-based constraints, which are designed for specific problems such as routing or scheduling.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about \"grid path\" optimization in this context, but they show that CP-SAT can be used with the routing solver through its backend support, though with limitations in the constraints it understands compared to the dedicated routing library.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2db57d10-e1b6-4d4f-941c-e20ad2249110","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:04.274Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d8c7be83-6066-4559-8c4d-0b9efbd27cf1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c4a399dc-93bf-4f83-9c69-41811ffdd6d4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01De3tSKDphesQT6byLdakfJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools SimpleMinCostFlow SimpleMaxFlow Python multi-commodity flow\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Minimum Cost Flows | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/flow/mincostflow\"},{\"title\":\"SimpleMinCostFlow | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/graph/min_cost_flow/SimpleMinCostFlow\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/graph/min_cost_flow.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/graph/min_cost_flow.h\"},{\"title\":\"A question on implementation of \\\"SimpleMinCostFlow()\\\" · Issue #562 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/562\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.graph.python.min_cost_flow API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/graph/python/min_cost_flow.html\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Minimum Cost Flow Problem\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/9ElT8PZZ2Mw\"},{\"title\":\"Maximum Flows | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/flow/maxflow\"},{\"title\":\"Minimum Cost Flow using NetworkX and OR-Tools\",\"url\":\"https://transport-systems.imperial.ac.uk/tf/60008_21/n3_5_minimum_cost_flow_ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"min_cost_flow | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/graph/min_cost_flow\"},{\"title\":\"SimpleMaxFlow | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/graph/max_flow/SimpleMaxFlow\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about OR-Tools' flow solvers. Here are the key findings:\n\n## SimpleMinCostFlow\n\nThe `SimpleMinCostFlow` class provides an interface for solving min-cost flow problems. Key actions include: `AddArcWithCapacityAndUnitCost` to define arcs with capacity and cost; `SetNodeSupply` to set node supplies/demands; `Solve` to find the minimum-cost flow, verifying supply/demand balance; `SolveMaxFlowWithMinCost` computes max flow with minimum cost and doesn't require to have supply and demand to be the same.\n\nIt is a simple and efficient min-cost flow interface that is as fast as GenericMinCostFlow<ReverseArcStaticGraph>, which is the fastest, but uses more memory in order to hide the somewhat involved construction of the static graph.\n\n## SimpleMaxFlow\n\nSimpleMaxFlow is a fast and efficient C++ class for solving maximum flow problems. It offers methods to add arcs, set capacities, and retrieve flow information. `Solve()` calculates the maximum flow between a source and sink node.\n\n## Python Usage\n\nThe Python API includes methods like `add_arcs_with_capacity_and_unit_cost`, `set_nodes_supplies`, `solve`, and `solve_max_flow_with_min_cost`.\n\n## Regarding Multi-Commodity Flow\n\nThe search results focus on SimpleMinCostFlow and SimpleMaxFlow for single-commodity flow problems. Multi-commodity flow is a more complex variant that OR-Tools can solve, but the search results don't contain specific details about built-in multi-commodity flow solvers in OR-Tools. These single-commodity solvers can be adapted for multi-commodity problems by careful network construction, though specialized solvers may be needed for more complex scenarios.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8991a13c-4f5e-4278-953d-42cb5fe9f9e6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:04.742Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c4a399dc-93bf-4f83-9c69-41811ffdd6d4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7503ab33-5b79-4ed3-819b-f12a4d91c8f2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P4DbiPxdRn8hKDF3sxNhxY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools MathOpt LP MIP unified interface CP-SAT integration\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools.math_opt.python.parameters.SolveParameters Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/python/classortools_1_1math__opt_1_1python_1_1parameters_1_1SolveParameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Solve Optimization Problems on Google Cloud Platform using Google’s OR API and OR-tools MathOpt | Ebrahim Pichka\",\"url\":\"https://epichka.com/blog/2024/ortools-mathopt/\"},{\"title\":\"MIP solver choice 2023 · google/or-tools · Discussion #3969\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3969\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/math_opt\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Solving a MIP Problem | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/mip/mip_example\"},{\"title\":\"Next major release will be 10.0 · google/or-tools · Discussion #3992\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3992\"},{\"title\":\"MIP aspects of OR-tools CP-SAT solver. Frederic Didier (fdid@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://www.mixedinteger.org/EUROMIP/2025/slides/frederic-didier.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about OR-Tools MathOpt LP MIP unified interface and CP-SAT integration:\n\n## MathOpt Overview\n\nMathOpt is a library for modeling and solving mathematical optimization problems, such as LPs and MIPs. It supports continuous or integer variables, linear/quadratic constraints and objectives, and specialized MIP/conic constraints.\n\n## Unified Interface\n\nUsers can switch between solvers like GLOP, PDLP, CP-SAT, SCIP, GLPK, Gurobi, and HiGHS, independently of the model's definition. This unified interface approach is a key feature of MathOpt.\n\n## CP-SAT Integration\n\nMathOpt acts as a modeling layer in OR-Tools that allows using CP-SAT as a backend solver, but also MIP solvers such as Gurobi or HiGHS.\n\nCP-SAT is Google's CP-SAT solver that supports problems where all variables are integer and bounded (or implied to be after presolve).\n\n## Solver Support\n\nThe MathOpt Service supports multiple solvers including GLOP (Google's Glop linear solver supporting LP with primal and dual simplex methods), PDLP (Google's PDLP solver supporting LP and convex diagonal quadratic objectives using first order methods), and CP-SAT.\n\nThe search results indicate that MathOpt provides a modern, flexible interface for mathematical optimization that abstracts away solver-specific details while still supporting CP-SAT and multiple other solvers as interchangeable backends.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6e977879-7cff-4782-a737-e918ef82de5c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:06.807Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7503ab33-5b79-4ed3-819b-f12a4d91c8f2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6f149351-3f8d-4e50-9fac-4b882f2bac60","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N9hCpycLbNko63Asoxyaeg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools network simplex algorithm min cost flow performance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Minimum Cost Flows | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/flow/mincostflow\"},{\"title\":\"Minimum Cost Flow using NetworkX and OR-Tools\",\"url\":\"https://transport-systems.imperial.ac.uk/tf/60008_21/n3_5_minimum_cost_flow_ortools\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/graph/min_cost_flow.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/graph/min_cost_flow.h\"},{\"title\":\"Minimum-cost flow problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minimum-cost_flow_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Assignment as a Minimum Cost Flow Problem | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/flow/assignment_min_cost_flow\"},{\"title\":\"Network simplex algorithm - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_simplex_algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"min_cost_flow | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/graph/min_cost_flow\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) An Application of Network Simplex Method For Minimum Cost Flow Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/258211247_An_Application_of_Network_Simplex_Method_For_Minimum_Cost_Flow_Problems\"},{\"title\":\"1 15.053 Tuesday, April 10 The Network Simplex Method for\",\"url\":\"https://dspace.mit.edu/bitstream/handle/1721.1/84610/15-053-spring-2007/contents/lecture-notes/lec15.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"networkx.algorithms.flow.mincost — NetworkX 3.6.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/_modules/networkx/algorithms/flow/mincost.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about OR-Tools, network simplex algorithm, and minimum cost flow performance:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe minimum cost flow problem seeks the most cost-efficient way to transport material through a network, minimizing total transportation costs while respecting node supplies, demands, and arc capacities.\n\n## Network Simplex Algorithm Performance\n\nThe minimum cost flow problem can be solved efficiently using the network simplex algorithm. The network simplex method works very well in practice, typically 200 to 300 times faster than the simplex method applied to general linear program of same dimensions.\n\nThe network simplex method is an adaptation of the bounded variable primal simplex algorithm, where the basis is represented as a rooted spanning tree of the underlying network, in which variables are represented by arcs, and the simplex multipliers by node potentials.\n\n## OR-Tools Implementation Details\n\nOR-Tools provides the `SimpleMinCostFlow` solver for solving minimum cost flow problems. Regarding the specific algorithm complexity, the complexity of the algorithm is O(n^2*m*log(n*C)) where C is the value of the largest arc cost in the graph.\n\nFeasibility checking is implemented using a max-flow, which has a much lower complexity, and the impact on performance is negligible, while the risk of being caught in an endless loop is removed.\n\nAdditionally, min cost flow can often return a solution faster than either the MIP or CP-SAT solver.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c34835a3-597a-48a5-9bfd-af3208c0ed8b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:09.072Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6f149351-3f8d-4e50-9fac-4b882f2bac60","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
