{"parentUuid":"325ace5a-f013-4154-9f28-4b1df1e4e650","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y6HUyjD8FH7S4WGYydpBok","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools constraint_solver legacy CP solver still maintained 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Original CP Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/routing/original_cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools: Google's Operations Research tools: · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"custom constraint or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/qANoFaIsj88\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Optimization | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/\"},{\"title\":\"ortools API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools: ortools/constraint_solver/docs/CP.md | Fossies\",\"url\":\"https://fossies.org/linux/or-tools/ortools/constraint_solver/docs/CP.md\"},{\"title\":\"ortools · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/ortools/\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OR-Tools\"},{\"title\":\"Google AI’s OR-Tools CP-SAT Solver unofficial tutorial Bobak Pezeshki\",\"url\":\"https://ics.uci.edu/~dechter/courses/ics-275/fall-2020/slides/OR-Tools_CP-SAT_Solver_Tutorial.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the OR-Tools legacy CP solver maintenance status:\n\nThe original constraint programming solver has been replaced by the superior CP-SAT solver, and Google strongly recommends using the CP-SAT solver rather than the original CP solver.\n\nHowever, the original CP solver is still maintained, but they will not work on it to improve performance, except for the routing library.\n\nAdditionally, the original CP solver is the foundation of the routing library, and its API may be necessary to customize a routing model.\n\nIn terms of the Python interface, the legacy Constraint Programming Solver is available as `ortools.constraint_solver.pywrapcp`. The documentation was last updated in March 2026, indicating active maintenance of the OR-Tools package overall.\n\nIn summary: while the legacy CP solver is still maintained and functional as of 2026, Google prioritizes the CP-SAT solver for most use cases and does not allocate resources to improve the legacy solver's performance, aside from maintaining it for the routing library.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1bcb6206-9c25-4946-8392-eec4c0dd076a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:17.626Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"325ace5a-f013-4154-9f28-4b1df1e4e650","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b8a075ba-4825-42a8-9837-3ca36c75b80c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HfnJY8cW6v1cV812SCuVVs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools Routing solver LNS routing_path_lns routing_random_lns operators\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/constraint_solver/routing_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/constraint_solver/routing_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"Routing Options | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/routing/routing_options\"},{\"title\":\"routing | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/constraint_solver/routing\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools/constraint_solver/routing.h File Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/cpp/routing_8h.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools\",\"url\":\"https://google.github.io/or-tools/cpp_routing/classoperations__research_1_1_base_lns.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/constraint_solver/routing.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/constraint_solver/routing.h\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools/constraint_solver/routing.cc File Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/cpp/routing_8cc.html\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: Google.OrTools.ConstraintSolver.RoutingSearchParameters Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/dotnet/classGoogle_1_1OrTools_1_1ConstraintSolver_1_1RoutingSearchParameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/src/constraint_solver/routing.h Source File - Doxy\",\"url\":\"https://lia.disi.unibo.it/Staff/MicheleLombardi/or-tools-doc/reference_manual/or-tools/src/constraint_solver/routing_8h-source.html\"},{\"title\":\"Optional node unnecessarily visited in OR-tools vehicle routing problem\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/hl2t_bIBrJI\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about OR-Tools Routing solver LNS operators:\n\n## LNS (Large Neighborhood Search) Operators in OR-Tools\n\nLNS (Large Neighborhood Search) can find good solutions but is usually very slow, and the LocalSearchOperators enum in constraint_solver.h contains more information about these operators.\n\n### Key LNS Operators\n\nThe `use_full_path_lns` operator relaxes one entire path and all inactive nodes.\n\n`use_tsp_lns` randomly merges consecutive nodes until n \"meta\"-nodes remain and solves the corresponding TSP, and to force diversification, the operator iteratively forces each node to serve as base of a meta-node.\n\n`use_inactive_lns` is an operator which relaxes all inactive nodes and one sub-chain of six consecutive arcs, allowing the path to be improved by inserting inactive nodes or swapping arcs.\n\n### Related Configuration\n\nThe routing solver offers various search limits like solution_limit, time_limit.seconds, and lns_time_limit.seconds to control the search process.\n\nThe search results indicate that while `routing_path_lns` and `routing_random_lns` are mentioned in your query, the detailed documentation in the results primarily covers the standard LNS operators through the `local_search_operators` configuration in the RoutingSearchParameters protocol buffer definition.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"785eb4d9-7bb3-4693-9455-2e0254f40f9f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:19.589Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b8a075ba-4825-42a8-9837-3ca36c75b80c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"70f1c12d-4347-4807-a5b9-e21a81552b42","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019wdcTvd6hecyZiYivYQgzG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools graph shortest path BFS DFS Python API ortools.graph\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Graph Algorithms in Python: BFS, DFS, and Beyond\",\"url\":\"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/graph-algorithms-in-python-bfs-dfs-and-beyond/\"},{\"title\":\"Breadth First Search or BFS for a Graph in Python - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/python/python-program-for-breadth-first-search-or-bfs-for-a-graph/\"},{\"title\":\"Deep path traversal algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://memgraph.com/docs/advanced-algorithms/deep-path-traversal\"},{\"title\":\"Lesson 5 - Graph Algorithms (BFS, DFS & Shortest Paths) | Jovian\",\"url\":\"https://jovian.ai/learn/data-structures-and-algorithms-in-python/lesson/lesson-5-graph-algorithms-bfs-dfs-shortest-paths\"},{\"title\":\"A self learner's guide to shortest path algorithms, with implementations in python. | Towards Data Science\",\"url\":\"https://towardsdatascience.com/a-self-learners-guide-to-shortest-path-algorithms-with-implementations-in-python-a084f60f43dc/\"},{\"title\":\"Shortest Path in Unweighted Undirected Graph using BFS\",\"url\":\"https://pencilprogrammer.com/algorithms/shortest-path-in-unweighted-graph-using-bfs/\"},{\"title\":\"Breadth First Search or BFS for a Graph - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/dsa/breadth-first-search-or-bfs-for-a-graph/\"},{\"title\":\"Shortest Path Algorithm in Unweighted Graph Using BFS\",\"url\":\"https://youcademy.org/graph-shortest-path-using-bfs/\"},{\"title\":\"Struggling with DFS and BFS ? Here’s the Ultimate Beginner’s Guide! | by Mahmoud Ayach | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@mahmoudayache2/struggling-with-dfs-and-bfs-heres-the-ultimate-beginner-s-guide-38d94bb9267b\"},{\"title\":\"Breadth-First Search in Python: A Guide with Examples | DataCamp\",\"url\":\"https://www.datacamp.com/tutorial/breadth-first-search-in-python\"}]\n\nI found search results about BFS, DFS, and shortest path algorithms in general, but the results don't contain specific information about Google's OR-Tools library (`ortools.graph`) Python API. The search results focus on general graph algorithm implementations rather than the OR-Tools framework.\n\nTo get information specifically about the OR-Tools graph module and its shortest path, BFS, and DFS capabilities, I'd recommend:\n\n1. **Official OR-Tools Documentation**: Visit https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/python/ortools.graph to see the official Python API reference for graph operations.\n\n2. **Key OR-Tools Graph Classes**: OR-Tools provides several relevant classes in the `ortools.graph` module:\n   - `routing.RoutingIndexManager` and `routing.RoutingModel` for vehicle routing problems\n   - Graph algorithms like shortest path solvers built on top of the core graph structures\n\n3. **GitHub Repository**: Check https://github.com/google/or-tools for example code and documentation on using graph algorithms.\n\nThe search results I retrieved were primarily about implementing BFS and DFS manually in Python rather than using specialized libraries like OR-Tools. If you need specific information about OR-Tools' graph API, its shortest path algorithms, or how it implements BFS/DFS, I'd recommend consulting the official documentation directly or searching for \"OR-Tools shortest path example Python\" or \"OR-Tools graph algorithms tutorial.\"\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9d7c8f9c-180a-4045-9583-73550c8b69ad","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:19.880Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"70f1c12d-4347-4807-a5b9-e21a81552b42","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"61d794d4-91b5-4eeb-aac6-b91504cba54a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013xegzPvUtGS7cmyTGa36V4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools LinearSumAssignment Hungarian algorithm Python\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/hungarian.h at v8.0 · google/or-tools · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v8.0/ortools/algorithms/hungarian.h\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/hungarian.h at master · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/algorithms/hungarian.h\"},{\"title\":\"hungarian | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.cn/optimization/reference/algorithms/hungarian\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/algorithms/hungarian.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/algorithms/hungarian.h\"},{\"title\":\"scipy.optimize.linear_sum_assignment — SciPy v1.2.0 Reference Guide\",\"url\":\"https://docs.scipy.org/doc//scipy-1.2.0/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.linear_sum_assignment.html\"},{\"title\":\"scipy.optimize.linear_sum_assignment — SciPy v0.18.1 Reference Guide\",\"url\":\"https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy-0.18.1/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.linear_sum_assignment.html\"},{\"title\":\"linear_sum_assignment — SciPy v1.17.0 Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.linear_sum_assignment.html\"},{\"title\":\"Principles and Applications of the Hungarian Algorithm: A Detailed Explanation of the Linear_sum_assignment Function - Oreate AI Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.oreateai.com/blog/principles-and-applications-of-the-hungarian-algorithm-a-detailed-explanation-of-the-linearsumassignment-function/65e1925a88f7e3ebad278b3829093f7d\"},{\"title\":\"Hungarian algorithm for preference maximization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://gist.github.com/jcheong0428/44babd453d2f762894db9724b041ba9c\"},{\"title\":\"hungarian-algorithm · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/hungarian-algorithm/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about OR-Tools LinearSumAssignment and the Hungarian algorithm in Python:\n\n## Overview\n\nOR-Tools contains an O(n^4) implementation of the Kuhn-Munkres algorithm (also known as the Hungarian algorithm) for solving the assignment problem. The algorithm takes a set of agents, a set of tasks, and a cost associated with assigning each agent to each task and produces an optimal (least cost) assignment.\n\n## LinearSumAssignment in OR-Tools\n\nFunctions like `MaximizeLinearAssignment` and `MinimizeLinearAssignment` compute the assignment and return results through `direct_assignment` and `reverse_assignment`. The code also enables computing a maximum assignment by changing the input matrix.\n\n## Python Alternatives\n\nFor Python users, the linear_sum_assignment function from the Scipy library is a specific implementation of this algorithm. The method used is the Hungarian algorithm, also known as the Munkres or Kuhn-Munkres algorithm.\n\nThe search results show that OR-Tools provides optimized implementations of the Hungarian algorithm in C++, while SciPy offers a Python-friendly alternative for solving linear sum assignment problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f78f8fbb-f74e-4c2f-b269-b25f79dca559","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:19.894Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"61d794d4-91b5-4eeb-aac6-b91504cba54a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
