{"parentUuid":"a0d7034d-f2d2-4861-a969-73075c769679","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019UK4KVxiqEq1KRXVz36CCm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Crwi8P3hdaJW39NewKErnZ","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://developers.google.com/optimization/routing/original_cp_solver","prompt":"What is the original CP solver in OR-Tools? How does it relate to routing library? Why is it still maintained? What features does it have that CP-SAT doesn't?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6628,"cache_read_input_tokens":25353,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6628,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":55,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox8TK5ZbQceVPB76a8B","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a151e6ec-128f-4d55-933c-f984d96433c6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:26.576Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a151e6ec-128f-4d55-933c-f984d96433c6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019UK4KVxiqEq1KRXVz36CCm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U966H7dQRuHyoiuXfJWMWa","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools","prompt":"What modules does OR-Tools provide? List the directory structure: graph, sat, constraint_solver, algorithms, math_opt. Which are exposed in Python?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6628,"cache_read_input_tokens":25353,"output_tokens":446,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6628},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":25353,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6628,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6628,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox8TK5ZbQceVPB76a8B","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a8069163-a86e-416f-b50c-5e977858a368","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:28.031Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a0d7034d-f2d2-4861-a969-73075c769679","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y5WM2xLyvGZdmcEwapFyN6","type":"tool_result","content":"# OR-Tools SimpleMinCostFlow API in Python\n\n## Overview\nThe SimpleMinCostFlow API is a solver for the minimum cost flow problem. According to the documentation, it seeks to find \"the most cost-efficient way to transport material through a network, minimizing total transportation costs while respecting node supplies, demands, and arc capacities.\"\n\n## Usage in Python\nYou instantiate it via:\n```python\nfrom ortools.graph.python import min_cost_flow\nsmcf = min_cost_flow.SimpleMinCostFlow()\n```\n\nYou define arcs with capacities and unit costs, set node supplies/demands, then call `solve()` to find the optimal flow distribution.\n\n## Algorithms\nThe documentation provided does not specify which underlying algorithms the solver implements.\n\n## Grid Path/Routing Problems\nSimpleMinCostFlow is **not designed for grid-based routing**. It solves network flow problems with explicit arc definitions. For actual routing and path-finding on grids, OR-Tools offers dedicated solutions like the routing library, which handles \"Traveling Salesperson Problem,\" \"Vehicle Routing Problem,\" and related variants.\n\n## Limitations vs CP-SAT for Routing\nThe documentation does not make direct comparisons between SimpleMinCostFlow and CP-SAT for routing. However, SimpleMinCostFlow is fundamentally a flow optimization tool, while CP-SAT is a constraint programming solver optimized for complex routing and scheduling problems with multiple constraints."}]},"uuid":"1f7c96af-0ccc-4741-98ec-aac279cd130e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:31.348Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a0d7034d-f2d2-4861-a969-73075c769679","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a151e6ec-128f-4d55-933c-f984d96433c6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Crwi8P3hdaJW39NewKErnZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# The Original CP Solver in OR-Tools\n\n## What It Is\nThe original CP solver is Google's foundational constraint programming solver that has been superseded by the more advanced CP-SAT solver. According to the documentation, it remains relevant as \"the foundation of the [routing library](/optimization/routing), and its API may be necessary to customize a routing model.\"\n\n## Relationship to Routing Library\nThe original CP solver serves as the underlying engine for OR-Tools' routing library. This connection is why it continues to be maintained—developers working with the routing library may need to access its API for customization purposes.\n\n## Why It's Still Maintained\nRather than being abandoned, the original solver is preserved specifically because of its integration with routing functionality. The documentation notes that while the CP-SAT solver is recommended for most tasks, the original CP solver remains relevant for those who require \"customization of a routing model.\"\n\n## Feature Comparison\nThe page doesn't detail features that the original CP solver possesses but CP-SAT lacks. Instead, it emphasizes that CP-SAT is superior, with a strong recommendation to use it: \"We **strongly** recommend using the [CP-SAT solver](/optimization/cp/cp_solver) rather than the original CP solver.\"\n\nThe original solver does feature a **decision builder** component that controls variable selection and value assignment strategies during search, though this functionality likely exists in CP-SAT as well."}]},"uuid":"76bbbf2e-423d-4982-9eb5-dd4a83e43b8b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:32.602Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a151e6ec-128f-4d55-933c-f984d96433c6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a8069163-a86e-416f-b50c-5e977858a368","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U966H7dQRuHyoiuXfJWMWa","type":"tool_result","content":"# OR-Tools Modules and Python Exposure\n\nBased on the GitHub repository content, OR-Tools provides several key modules:\n\n## Directory Structure\n\nThe repository includes these main components:\n\n- **graph** - Graph algorithms (shortest paths, min cost flow, max flow, linear sum assignment)\n- **sat** - SAT solver with CP-SAT constraint programming\n- **constraint_solver** - Constraint and Routing solver\n- **algorithms** - Basic algorithms including bin packing and knapsack\n- **linear_solver** - Linear solver wrapper\n- **glop** - Simplex-based linear programming solver\n- **pdlp** - First-order linear programming solver\n\nThe documentation mentions \"Two constraint programming solver (CP\\* and CP-SAT); Two linear programming solvers (Glop and PDLP)\" as core offerings.\n\n## Python Exposure\n\nThe repository confirms that OR-Tools provides \"wrappers in Python, C# and Java.\" While the page lists example directories for Python, it does not specify which individual modules are exposed in the Python bindings. The structure suggests core functionality is wrapped, but complete Python API coverage isn't detailed in this excerpt.\n\nThe project is written primarily in C++ (79.1%) with Python comprising 6.3% of the codebase."}]},"uuid":"04c31401-2bc8-4d5c-a6cf-0916a8a7fa58","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:33.888Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a8069163-a86e-416f-b50c-5e977858a368","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
