{"parentUuid":"d6fcdb6f-938f-491c-b8e4-6a06518406aa","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01M6hb1vJEFaUx4n2QnuYWRA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0142wiFNgwmbvfuiV7zH1U5S","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/graph/python/min_cost_flow.html","prompt":"List all Python API methods on SimpleMinCostFlow. What arguments does add_arcs_with_capacity_and_unit_cost take? Any batch APIs? How is solve called?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1933,"cache_read_input_tokens":31981,"output_tokens":342,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1933},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":31981,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1933,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox9Ukg87Xp6oP8AwVPM","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6cc051ad-e1ad-40a3-a6a4-ad390da96e59","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:39.438Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"44fb49f9-3a23-4c5e-973d-1cee7b878b3c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011g5PZ7cF1EzSJA8r7ZZbou","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools routing model add_circuit Hamiltonian path grid TSP CP-SAT constraint\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"How to implement a circuit constraint ?\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Tv9TSXVSpLg\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/constraint_solver/routing_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/constraint_solver/routing_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"routing: gives bad solutions for hamiltonian path problems · Issue #247 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/247\"},{\"title\":\"Vehicle Routing with modified distance matrix does not compute objective function correctly? · Issue #3820 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3820\"},{\"title\":\"hamiltonian_path | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/graph/hamiltonian_path\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Cut generators in CPModelProto · Issue #912 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/912\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/constraint_solver/routing.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/constraint_solver/routing.h\"},{\"title\":\"multiple TSP with direct constraints\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/NxG0VIYLiiA\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for your query about OR-Tools routing model, add_circuit, Hamiltonian path, grid TSP, and CP-SAT constraints. Here are the relevant results:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**add_circuit Constraint for TSP/Circuit Problems:**\n\nThe add_circuit constraint is used to solve circuit problems within directed graphs by taking a list of triples (u,v,var), where u and v denote the source and target vertices, and var is a Boolean variable that indicates if an edge is included in the solution, ensuring that the edges marked as True form a single circuit visiting each vertex exactly once.\n\n**Advantages of add_circuit:**\n\nThe add_circuit constraint can utilize lazy constraints internally, offering a substantial advantage in solving the TSP. Both the Dantzig-Fulkerson-Johnson (DFJ) and Miller-Tucker-Zemlin (MTZ) formulations perform significantly worse than the add_circuit constraint.\n\n**Related Constraints:**\n\nFor problems involving multiple trips starting from a depot, the add_multiple_circuit constraint can be used, which is similar to add_circuit but explicitly allows the depot to be visited multiple times, and is particularly useful for modeling Vehicle Routing Problems (VRP).\n\n**Hamiltonian Path in OR-Tools:**\n\nOR-Tools provides a complete algorithm for solving the Shortest Hamiltonian Path Problem using dynamic programming based on the Held-Karp algorithm, which calculates the optimal path visiting all nodes once, with time complexity O(n^2 * 2^(n-1)) and space complexity O(n * 2^(n-1)).\n\nThe search results show that the add_circuit constraint is a powerful feature in OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver for handling tour and path problems on graphs, with superior performance compared to manual formulations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9268690b-ba17-477d-96d0-dda1a21e8490","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:44.483Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"44fb49f9-3a23-4c5e-973d-1cee7b878b3c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6cc051ad-e1ad-40a3-a6a4-ad390da96e59","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0142wiFNgwmbvfuiV7zH1U5S","type":"tool_result","content":"# SimpleMinCostFlow Python API Methods\n\n## All Methods\n\n- `__init__()` - Constructor\n- `add_arc_with_capacity_and_unit_cost()` - Single arc addition\n- `add_arcs_with_capacity_and_unit_cost()` - Batch arc addition\n- `set_arc_capacity()` - Single arc capacity update\n- `set_arc_capacities()` - Batch capacity update\n- `set_node_supply()` - Single node supply setting\n- `set_nodes_supplies()` - Batch supply setting\n- `num_nodes()` - Get node count\n- `num_arcs()` - Get arc count\n- `tail()` - Get arc source node\n- `head()` - Get arc destination node\n- `capacity()` - Get arc capacity\n- `supply()` - Get node supply\n- `unit_cost()` - Get arc unit cost\n- `solve()` - Standard solve\n- `solve_max_flow_with_min_cost()` - Max flow variant\n- `optimal_cost()` - Get result cost\n- `maximum_flow()` - Get total flow\n- `flow()` - Get single arc flow\n- `flows()` - Get multiple arc flows\n\n## add_arcs_with_capacity_and_unit_cost Arguments\n\nThis method accepts four numpy array parameters:\n- `tails: numpy.ndarray[numpy.int32]`\n- `heads: numpy.ndarray[numpy.int32]`\n- `capacities: numpy.ndarray[numpy.int64]`\n- `unit_costs: numpy.ndarray[numpy.int64]`\n\n## Batch APIs\n\nYes—batch operations include `add_arcs_with_capacity_and_unit_cost()`, `set_arc_capacities()`, `set_nodes_supplies()`, and `flows()`.\n\n## Solve Invocation\n\n\"`solve()` is called without parameters and returns a Status object indicating solution quality."}]},"uuid":"9fe5b32a-2b92-400a-bdc9-f8f850e6feb4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:44.699Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6cc051ad-e1ad-40a3-a6a4-ad390da96e59","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d6fcdb6f-938f-491c-b8e4-6a06518406aa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MQGwXGu58gGRZzz6FCjmB3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"multi-commodity flow\" OR-Tools CP-SAT vs LP solver comparison performance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding performance loss of solving my model with SatSolver in comparison to CspSolver · Issue #1028 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1028\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT poor performance\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/tmF6DmQBYU4\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"MIP solver choice 2023 · google/or-tools · Discussion #3969\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3969\"},{\"title\":\"Google's OR-Tools and CP-SAT versus Commercial Solvers, esp. Gurobi | INFORMS Open Forum\",\"url\":\"https://connect.informs.org/discussion/googles-or-tools-and-cp-sat-versus-commercial-solvers-esp-gurobi\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding OR-Tools CP-SAT and LP solver comparisons:\n\n## Key Performance Characteristics\n\nThe CP-SAT solver is designed for integer programming problems and is generally faster than MPSolver. However, there are important tradeoffs to consider:\n\n**When LP Solvers May Be Better:**\n\nUnlike MIP/LP-solvers, CP-SAT lacks support for continuous variables, and in cases where your problem predominantly features continuous variables and linear constraints, opting for an LP-solver is likely to yield significantly improved performance.\n\n**CP-SAT Advantages:**\n\nAs a portfolio solver, CP-SAT concurrently executes a multitude of diverse algorithms and strategies, each possessing unique strengths and weaknesses. These elements operate largely independently but engage in information exchange, sharing progress when better solutions emerge or tighter bounds become available. While this may initially appear as an inefficient approach due to potential redundancy, it proves highly effective in practice.\n\n## Specific Considerations for Multi-Commodity Flow\n\nThe search results don't contain specific benchmarks for multi-commodity flow problems comparing CP-SAT directly to LP solvers. However, since multi-commodity flow problems typically involve continuous variables and linear constraints, the general guidance suggests that an LP-solver is likely to yield significantly improved performance for such problems.\n\nFor more specific performance comparisons on multi-commodity flow problems, you may need to consult specialized literature or conduct empirical benchmarks on your specific problem instances.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7496a5b0-6375-4ec8-bab1-9ba7f74b8168","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:45.306Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d6fcdb6f-938f-491c-b8e4-6a06518406aa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7496a5b0-6375-4ec8-bab1-9ba7f74b8168","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DUma9E1qkbkxBirg4pkezm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ushv2QtTznWnwUPuAAf1iA","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/graph/min_cost_flow.h","prompt":"What algorithm does GenericMinCostFlow use? Cost-scaling push-relabel? Network simplex? What is the complexity? What are the limitations on integer cost?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":674,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3149,"cache_read_input_tokens":33914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3149,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":57,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxAKYZmn69Z6UUnxzGd","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f4b62321-37e7-4d49-b4c7-d55b929a9302","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:48.854Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f4b62321-37e7-4d49-b4c7-d55b929a9302","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DUma9E1qkbkxBirg4pkezm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013tkNGbJs3gzRBoBryRUrDh","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CaDiCaL IPASIR-UP CP-SAT external solver vs OR-Tools internal modules engineering effort"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":674,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3149,"cache_read_input_tokens":33914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3149,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":57,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxAKYZmn69Z6UUnxzGd","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"43e7f22f-b4ef-4de0-9016-6ac50ca8b1a8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:49.990Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"43e7f22f-b4ef-4de0-9016-6ac50ca8b1a8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DUma9E1qkbkxBirg4pkezm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DGm2uALAvHLUJKBANBTgxU","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html","prompt":"What does add_circuit do? What does add_multiple_circuit do? Performance compared to manual MTZ formulation? Can these be used for grid path routing?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":674,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3149,"cache_read_input_tokens":33914,"output_tokens":412,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3149},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":674,"output_tokens":412,"cache_read_input_tokens":33914,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3149,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3149,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxAKYZmn69Z6UUnxzGd","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9041eb64-baf0-4e9c-a672-dfdacd8564a9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:51.678Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f4b62321-37e7-4d49-b4c7-d55b929a9302","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ushv2QtTznWnwUPuAAf1iA","type":"tool_result","content":"# GenericMinCostFlow Algorithm Details\n\n**Algorithm:** GenericMinCostFlow implements a \"cost-scaling push-relabel algorithm for the min-cost flow problem.\"\n\n**Complexity:** The algorithm has a complexity of O(n²·m·log(n·C)), where n is the number of nodes, m is the number of arcs, and C represents the maximum absolute arc cost value.\n\n**Integer Cost Limitations:** The implementation handles integer costs through a scaling mechanism. \"If the arc costs are integers, and epsilon < 1/n, any epsilon-optimal flow is optimal.\" To achieve this, the algorithm multiplies all arc costs and initial epsilon by (n+1), ensuring that when epsilon reaches 1, the solution becomes truly optimal rather than merely approximate.\n\n**Key Constraints:**\n- The algorithm cannot independently detect infeasibility and may loop indefinitely without a feasibility check\n- Feasibility checking is enabled by default using a max-flow approach\n- Integer overflow can occur if arc costs times (num_nodes + 1) exceed int64_t limits\n- Arc capacities must not cause overflow in node excess calculations"}]},"uuid":"7b78cc88-374d-44c4-9370-4dbdc86f6981","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:54.103Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f4b62321-37e7-4d49-b4c7-d55b929a9302","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9041eb64-baf0-4e9c-a672-dfdacd8564a9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"39d21099-a8f4-47b7-adde-933641c1bb9e","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DGm2uALAvHLUJKBANBTgxU","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Circuit Constraints Summary\n\n## add_circuit\nThis constraint solves circuit problems in directed graphs. It takes triples of (source, target, boolean_variable) and ensures selected edges form \"a single circuit visiting each vertex exactly once, aside from vertices with a loop set as True.\"\n\n## add_multiple_circuit\nThis variant allows multiple disjoint tours and \"explicitly allows the depot to be visited multiple times.\" It's particularly useful for Vehicle Routing Problems where multiple trips originate from a single depot.\n\n## Performance vs. MTZ Formulation\nThe document indicates that both the Dantzig-Fulkerson-Johnson and Miller-Tucker-Zemlin formulations \"perform significantly worse than the add_circuit constraint.\" The key advantage: \"Unlike end users, the add_circuit constraint can utilize lazy constraints internally.\"\n\nPerformance on TSPLIB instances shows add_circuit achieving optimality on instances up to ~200 nodes within time limits, though specialized TSP solvers remain superior.\n\n## Grid Path Routing\nThe primer doesn't directly address grid-based routing. However, it notes these constraints extend \"far beyond traditional routing issues\" and can model \"scenarios that require multiple disjoint sub-tours.\" The document suggests considering \"OR-Tools Routing if routing constitutes a significant aspect of your problem,\" suggesting add_circuit may not be optimal for specialized grid routing applications."}]},"uuid":"dfe49618-e701-418f-b633-fc8882ef6d59","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:57.411Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9041eb64-baf0-4e9c-a672-dfdacd8564a9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"43e7f22f-b4ef-4de0-9016-6ac50ca8b1a8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"39d21099-a8f4-47b7-adde-933641c1bb9e","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013tkNGbJs3gzRBoBryRUrDh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL IPASIR-UP CP-SAT external solver vs OR-Tools internal modules engineering effort\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ipasir2/ipasir2_solver_cadical: CaDiCaL SAT Solver with IPASIR 2 Support · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ipasir2/ipasir2_solver_cadical\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/src/cadical.hpp at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/src/cadical.hpp\"},{\"title\":\"Incremental Inprocessing in SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://abs.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/2019/FBS_2019.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL(T ): CaDiCaL as CDCL(T ) Engine in cvc5\",\"url\":\"https://cs.stanford.edu/~preiner/talks/Preiner-Shonan23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Deep Integration of SAT Solving and Model Checking\",\"url\":\"https://froleyks.de/assets/pdf/Deep%20integration%20of%20SAT%20solving%20and%20model%20checking.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/NEWS.md at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/NEWS.md\"},{\"title\":\"Solver in cadical - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cadical/latest/cadical/struct.Solver.html\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/cadical: CaDiCaL SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about CaDiCaL and IPASIR-UP. Now let me search for information specifically comparing external solver integration versus OR-Tools internal modules:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Google AI’s OR-Tools CP-SAT Solver unofficial tutorial Bobak Pezeshki\",\"url\":\"https://ics.uci.edu/~dechter/courses/ics-275/fall-2020/slides/OR-Tools_CP-SAT_Solver_Tutorial.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Yes, OR-tools has a lot of solvers. The solver I talked about is the CP-SAT solv... | Hacker News\",\"url\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=32807583\"},{\"title\":\"description_or-tools_cp-sat.txt\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/description_or-tools_cp-sat.txt\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can now provide you with information about the comparison between external solver integration (CaDiCaL with IPASIR-UP) and OR-Tools' internal module approach:\n\n## CaDiCaL IPASIR-UP vs OR-Tools CP-SAT: Engineering Effort Comparison\n\n### CaDiCaL with IPASIR-UP External Solver Approach\n\nThe extension to add IPASIR-UP (external propagator support) to CaDiCaL required approximately 800 lines of C++ code in CaDiCaL, accompanied with another approximately 700 lines in its model based tester. This demonstrates a relatively modest engineering effort for adding external propagation capabilities to an existing SAT solver.\n\nThe IPASIR-UP interface provides advantages for enumeration tasks, where the current trail is preserved and backtracked, unlike the standard IPASIR interface which starts the search at the root level after a model has been found.\n\n### OR-Tools CP-SAT Internal Modules Approach\n\nIn contrast, OR-Tools takes an integrated approach with internal modules. The CP-SAT solver is architectured around five components: the base layer is a clause learning SAT solver; above the SAT layer sits a Constraint Programming (CP) module with Boolean, integer and interval variables, and standard integer, scheduling and routing constraints; alongside the CP solver, a simplex provides a global linear relaxation.\n\nThe integration of the CP and SAT layers enable the CP-SAT solver to solve MIP problems with the same techniques as commercial MIP solvers: relaxation, cuts, heuristics and duality based techniques.\n\n### Key Difference\n\nThe fundamental difference is architectural: CaDiCaL's IPASIR-UP allows external systems to inject domain knowledge during solving with minimal code changes, while OR-Tools CP-SAT implements all major components (SAT, CP, LP relaxation) internally as tightly integrated modules, requiring substantial engineering effort but providing comprehensive control over interactions between components.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4704f6f3-7c63-45ab-b3cb-121f8847514f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:59.155Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"43e7f22f-b4ef-4de0-9016-6ac50ca8b1a8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","se