{"parentUuid":"74b6a734-01dd-443e-ab86-08b55ef23495","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SW4JQDzr7crxQnEHTDHheu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PcW73S4RzMTwcb2j85Ln3U","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://developers.google.com/optimization/routing/routing_options","prompt":"What LNS operators does the Routing solver support? What are the local_search_operators options? How do they differ from CP-SAT LNS?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":524,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3816,"cache_read_input_tokens":37063,"output_tokens":350,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3816},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":524,"output_tokens":350,"cache_read_input_tokens":37063,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3816,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxBLmGXeNh6W2DPhzB6","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"be5945e0-baa7-41b4-b485-f67e00a01531","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:54:05.011Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"053230fc-a523-427e-96f5-d95cfb3c55e9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"39d21099-a8f4-47b7-adde-933641c1bb9e","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QMRwiKu9GQQ6yhR4vkGbpe","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools graph \"shortest_paths_via_dijkstra\" \"ortools.graph\" Python API\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"DijkstraShortestPath directly in python · Issue #1734 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1734\"},{\"title\":\"Using Google's OR-Tools to solve the shortest path problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/using-googles-or-tools-solve-shortest-path-problem-chapman-phd\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR Tools TSP solver Shortest path — allocator 0.1.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://allocator.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tsp_ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"shortestpaths | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/graph/shortestpaths\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools: Google's Operations Research tools: · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"Dijkstra missing in C#, Java & Python · Issue #75 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/75\"},{\"title\":\"Shortest Path (Dijkstra's) algorithm step-by-step Python guide | Towards Data Science\",\"url\":\"https://towardsdatascience.com/shortest-path-dijkstras-algorithm-step-by-step-python-guide-896769522752/\"},{\"title\":\"Dijkstra, Dantzig, and Shortest Paths - Spaghetti Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://stegua.github.io/blog/2012/09/19/dijkstra/\"},{\"title\":\"Dijkstar\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/Dijkstar/\"},{\"title\":\"Implementing Djikstra’s Shortest Path Algorithm with Python – Ben Alex Keen\",\"url\":\"https://benalexkeen.com/implementing-djikstras-shortest-path-algorithm-with-python/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools shortest path functionality:\n\nOR-Tools contains various shortest paths utilities including Dijkstra algorithms for directed graphs. The documentation indicates that OR-Tools provides utilities for finding shortest paths in a graph, including algorithms like Dijkstra's, A*, Bellman-Ford, and a stable variant of Dijkstra's.\n\nFor Python usage, the `ortools.graph.DijkstraShortestPath` function takes parameters including node_count, start_node, end_node, graph, and disconnected_distance.\n\nHowever, I should note that OR-Tools is written in C++ but provides wrappers in Python, C# and Java. The official reference documentation is available at the Google Developers site under the shortestpaths module in the graph package.\n\nFor more detailed API documentation, you can visit the official OR-Tools reference page at `developers.google.com/optimization/reference/graph/shortestpaths`.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a17da4b0-28d9-407c-9b40-3bd3fdaf73f6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:54:07.098Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"053230fc-a523-427e-96f5-d95cfb3c55e9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"be5945e0-baa7-41b4-b485-f67e00a01531","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"39d21099-a8f4-47b7-adde-933641c1bb9e","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PcW73S4RzMTwcb2j85Ln3U","type":"tool_result","content":"# Routing Solver LNS Operators\n\nBased on the provided documentation, **the page does not contain information about specific LNS (Large Neighborhood Search) operators supported by the Routing solver, nor does it list `local_search_operators` options.**\n\nThe document does discuss \"Local search options\" (metaheuristics), which are different from LNS operators. These include strategies like:\n\n- **GREEDY_DESCENT** - \"Accepts improving (cost-reducing) local search neighbors until a local minimum is reached\"\n- **GUIDED_LOCAL_SEARCH** - Uses guided local search to escape local minima\n- **SIMULATED_ANNEALING** - Employs simulated annealing techniques\n- **TABU_SEARCH** - Uses tabu search methods\n\nThese metaheuristics represent search *strategies* rather than specific LNS *operators* (which typically modify partial solutions by relaxing and re-optimizing portions of them).\n\nThe page also makes no comparison with CP-SAT LNS capabilities. To answer your questions about specific LNS operators and their differences from CP-SAT, you would need to consult additional OR-Tools documentation."}]},"uuid":"9b46eb20-04e2-47e1-a1db-b3df3c6e70ec","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:54:09.228Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"be5945e0-baa7-41b4-b485-f67e00a01531","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
