{"parentUuid":"eb40b19b-ff01-4635-b56e-a89c28cf08bc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01LJrcck2ak6KbCFAjVnZWxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MtUws645xRUWMhjqAi9Mz3","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"add_circuit\" CP-SAT performance \"subtour elimination\" lazy constraints grid routing"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":221,"cache_read_input_tokens":43275,"output_tokens":97,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":221},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":97,"cache_read_input_tokens":43275,"cache_creation_input_tokens":221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":221,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxCUQRsDS3adDR8esnx","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"582e8b3b-d1ec-41ee-a59d-c3318f052132","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:54:17.415Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"582e8b3b-d1ec-41ee-a59d-c3318f052132","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"44e8b644-8315-4e65-b71c-e25b0edf0dd8","agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtUws645xRUWMhjqAi9Mz3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"add_circuit\" CP-SAT performance \"subtour elimination\" lazy constraints grid routing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Subtour Elimination with lazy constraints\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/aimms/c/NLhuP7Ok0Fw\"},{\"title\":\"Kinda Technical | A Guide to Constraint Programming - CP-SAT Solver in OR-Tools\",\"url\":\"https://kindatechnical.com/constraint-programming/lesson-28-cp-sat-solver-in-or-tools.html\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint-based solution methods for vehicle routing problems\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/EWO_seminar_van_Hoeve.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Solve with Lazy Constraints — AIMMS How-To\",\"url\":\"https://how-to.aimms.com/Articles/126/126-TSP-Lazy-Constraints.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Location Routing Problem - Lazy Subtour Elimination Constraints – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/4410235441681-Location-Routing-Problem-Lazy-Subtour-Elimination-Constraints\"},{\"title\":\"How to implement a circuit constraint ?\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Tv9TSXVSpLg\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query about \"add_circuit\" CP-SAT performance with subtour elimination, lazy constraints, and grid routing. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Key Results:\n\nThe `add_circuit` constraint can utilize lazy constraints internally, offering a substantial advantage in solving the TSP, unlike traditional mathematical formulations.\n\nThe DFJ (Dantzig-Fulkerson-Johnson) formulation is generally more efficient due to its stronger linear relaxation, but requires lazy constraints which are not supported by CP-SAT. When implemented without lazy constraints, the DFJ formulation's performance is comparable to the MTZ formulation in CP-SAT. Nevertheless, both formulations perform significantly worse than the `add_circuit` constraint.\n\nThe `add_circuit` constraint is utilized to solve circuit problems within directed graphs by taking a list of triples (u,v,var) where u and v denote source and target vertices, and var indicates if an edge is included. The constraint ensures that the edges marked as True form a single circuit visiting each vertex exactly once.\n\nRegarding routing limitations, CP-SAT can model simplified vehicle routing but lacks native support for routing-specific constraints like subtour elimination and capacity propagation, which specialized solvers handle more efficiently.\n\nThe search results primarily focus on the superiority of `add_circuit` for TSP problems and explain how subtour elimination constraints work in general optimization frameworks, with emphasis on lazy constraint callbacks in commercial solvers like Gurobi and CPLEX.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fe19a61a-483b-45b1-a966-bc9da27e02b1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:54:24.403Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"582e8b3b-d1ec-41ee-a59d-c3318f052132","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fe19a61a-483b-45b1-a966-bc9da27e02b1","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5e5d808402d6e43d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Fw3gZVhDybywySfLvdepau","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough to write a comprehensive report. Let me now compile the findings.\n\n# OR-Tools 内部模块协同调研报告\n\n## 1. OR-Tools 模块横向对比\n\n| 模块 | Python 入口 | 算法 | 适用问题 | 跟 routing_subproblem 的匹配度 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **CP-SAT** | `ortools.sat.python.cp_model` | SAT + CP + LP relaxation 组合 | 整数变量 + 任意约束 | 当前基线，灵活但慢 |\n| **Routing solver** (legacy CP) | `ortools.constraint_solver.pywrapcp` + `routing_enums_pb2` | 基于老 CP solver + LNS + 元启发式 | VRP / TSP / 多车场 | **不直接适用网格路径**（要构造距离矩阵 + Hamiltonian 化） |\n| **Graph: SimpleMinCostFlow** | `ortools.graph.python.min_cost_flow` | cost-scaling push-relabel，复杂度 O(n²·m·log(n·C)) | 单商品最小费用流 | 高（如能拆分成单商品） |\n| **Graph: SimpleMaxFlow** | `ortools.graph.python.max_flow` | push-relabel | 最大流 / 可行性检查 | 中（仅可行性诊断） |\n| **Graph: LinearSumAssignment** | `ortools.graph.python.linear_sum_assignment` | Kuhn-Munkres O(n⁴) | 二分图最优匹配 | 低（结构不符） |\n| **Graph: shortest path** | `ortools.graph.pywrapgraph.DijkstraShortestPath` 等 | Dijkstra / Bellman-Ford / A* | 单源/多源最短路径 | 高（单条线路独立寻路） |\n| **MathOpt** | `ortools.math_opt.python` | 后端可切 GLOP/PDLP/CP-SAT/HiGHS/Gurobi/SCIP | LP/MIP 统一接口 | 中（适合 LP 松弛） |\n| **GLOP** | linear_solver | primal/dual simplex | 纯 LP | 中（多商品流 LP 松弛） |\n| **PDLP** | linear_solver | first-order | 大规模 LP | 中（百万级 LP） |\n| **CP-SAT add_circuit** | cp_model `AddCircuit` / `AddMultipleCircuit` | 内部 lazy subtour elimination | TSP / 单回路 | 高（替换 MTZ 公式可显著提速） |\n\n关键事实：\n- OR-Tools **没有专用 multi-commodity flow solver**。MCF 必须靠 GLOP/PDLP（LP 松弛）+ 整数化，或继续用 CP-SAT。\n- Routing solver 后端可挂 CP-SAT，但官方明确说：`CP-SAT does not grab additional constraints and does not yet understand all that can be expressed with just the RoutingModel`，且 `local search part is geared towards not calling the CP solver`，所以加速增益有限。\n- Network simplex：OR-Tools 文档没明确实现，主要是 **cost-scaling push-relabel**（`GenericMinCostFlow`）。文档原话：\"min cost flow can often return a solution faster than either the MIP or CP-SAT solver\"。\n\n## 2. 针对 routing_subproblem 的具体替换方案\n\n按工程量从小到大：\n\n**方案 A：CP-SAT 内部 `AddCircuit` 升级**（工程量最小，~1 天）\n- 当前 routing_subproblem 如果用 MTZ / DFJ 手工子回路消除，直接换 `model.AddCircuit([(u, v, lit), ...])`\n- 收益：内部 lazy subtour elimination + reified Boolean，TSPLIB 上 200 节点级别可达最优\n- 风险：仍是 CP-SAT，跟 master 同进程，并未摆脱 CP-SAT 主路径\n\n**方案 B：单线路用 Graph shortest path**（工程量中，~3-5 天）\n- 把每条传送带视为一条独立 source→sink 寻路，调用 `DijkstraShortestPath`\n- 障碍物（已占格、其他线路）作为不可走节点\n- 收益：纯 C++ 单源最短路径，毫秒级\n- 风险：**忽略多线路冲突**，要外加冲突检测 + 回退策略；本质退化为顺序贪心，会牺牲全局最优\n\n**方案 C：GLOP/PDLP 解 LP 松弛 + CP-SAT 整数化**（工程量大，~1-2 周）\n- 多商品流 LP 松弛交给 GLOP（simplex）或 PDLP（first-order，百万级也能跑）\n- 整数解用 CP-SAT 在 LP 提示基础上修复\n- 通过 MathOpt 切换后端\n- 收益：连续变量主导的 MCF，LP solver 比 CP-SAT 快一个量级\n- 风险：连续解到整数解的 rounding/CG cuts 要自己写\n\n**方案 D：Routing solver 接管**（工程量最大，~2-3 周，且不推荐）\n- 把网格转成节点 + 距离矩阵给 RoutingModel\n- 收益：现成的 LNS（`use_full_path_lns`、`use_inactive_lns`、`use_tsp_lns`）+ 元启发式（GLS、SA、TS）\n- 风险：legacy CP solver、网格 N×N 节点数爆炸、Routing 是 vehicle 中心抽象不天然适配格点路径\n\n## 3. Routing solver LNS 能否借给 CP-SAT 当前 LNS\n\n不能直接借。Routing solver 的 LNS 跑在老 CP solver 上，跟 CP-SAT 的 LNS（基于 SAT 重启 + 邻域）实现机制完全不同。CP-SAT 自己有 LNS（`SearchForAllSolutions` + `linearization_level`、`use_lns_only` 之类参数），Round 2 提到的 `routing_path_lns`、`routing_random_lns` 是 Routing 配置，挪不过来。\n\n## 4. legacy constraint_solver 价值\n\n官方表态：\"**will not work on it to improve performance, except for the routing library**\"。除非需要 Routing solver 的 callback 自定义，没有保留价值。\n\n## 5. 跟 D' (CaDiCaL+IPASIR-UP) 路径对比\n\n| 维度 | OR-Tools 内部模块路径 | CaDiCaL+IPASIR-UP 外部路径 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 工程量 | A 方案 1 天 / B 3-5 天 / C 1-2 周 | IPASIR-UP 集成 ~800 行 C++ + 适配，2-4 周 |\n| 风险 | 低（同生态、Python 直接可用） | 高（C++、外部依赖、Python 绑定要自写） |\n| 收益上限 | 中（受 CP-SAT 架构限制） | 高（可注入领域传播器，理论加速大） |\n| 可逆性 | 高（随时切回 CP-SAT） | 低（耦合深） |\n\n## 6. 可行性结论\n\n**用 OR-Tools 内部模块替换 routing_subproblem 是高可行性、低风险的方案**，建议执行顺序：\n\n1. **立即做**：方案 A（`AddCircuit`），前提是当前实现确实有 MTZ/DFJ 子回路约束。一天内出结果，几乎零风险。\n2. **短期试点**：方案 B（DijkstraShortestPath 单线路寻路），作为 routing_subproblem 的快速预解器 / warm start，为 CP-SAT 提供初始解 hints。\n3. **中期评估**：方案 C（GLOP/PDLP 解 MCF LP 松弛），针对 flow_subproblem 诊断阶段。`ortools.graph.python.min_cost_flow.SimpleMinCostFlow` 在单商品诊断上可直接秒杀当前 CP-SAT 实现。\n4. **不建议**：方案 D（Routing solver），抽象不匹配。\n\n跟 D'（CaDiCaL+IPASIR-UP）比，OR-Tools 内部模块路径**工程量小一个数量级、风险低一个量级，应优先尝试**；D' 留作 A/B/C 都走完仍卡瓶颈时的核选项。\n\n## 关键文档链接\n\nSources:\n- [CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools](https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver)\n- [Original CP Solver | OR-Tools](https://developers.google.com/optimization/routing/original_cp_solver)\n- [Minimum Cost Flows | OR-Tools](https://developers.google.com/optimization/flow/mincostflow)\n- [SimpleMinCostFlow Reference](https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/graph/min_cost_flow/SimpleMinCostFlow)\n- [ortools.graph.python.min_cost_flow API](https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/graph/python/min_cost_flow.html)\n- [Maximum Flows | OR-Tools](https://developers.google.com/optimization/flow/maxflow)\n- [hamiltonian_path | OR-Tools Reference](https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/graph/hamiltonian_path)\n- [hungarian | OR-Tools Reference](https://developers.google.cn/optimization/reference/algorithms/hungarian)\n- [MathOpt | OR-Tools](https://developers.google.com/optimization/math_opt)\n- [Routing Options | OR-Tools](https://developers.google.com/optimization/routing/routing_options)\n- [routing_parameters.proto on GitHub](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/constraint_solver/routing_parameters.proto)\n- [min_cost_flow.h on GitHub](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/graph/min_cost_flow.h)\n- [CP-SAT Primer: Advanced Modeling (add_circuit)](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html)\n- [Laurent Perron - CP-SAT and OR-Tools (PDF)](https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf)\n- [MIP aspects of OR-tools CP-SAT (Frederic Didier, EUROMIP 2025 PDF)](https://www.mixedinteger.org/EUROMIP/2025/slides/frederic-didier.pdf)\n- [IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL (DROPS)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8)\n- [The CP-SAT solution in VRP Routing Solver is not returned (Issue #4439)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4439)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1524,"cache_read_input_tokens":43496,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1524,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxDCfuP6m39XLSmW9ZV","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"79a0901a-9271-4be0-acf1-dcec6c0dc00c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:55:26.822Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
